  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Prior to the first\noccupation of any of the flats hereby approved, the refuse and recycling\nstorage facilities shown on Drawing No. 2611/02 Rev A (Landscaping Plan, June\n2026) shall be provided in full and thereafter retained and kept available for\nrefuse and recycling storage purposes.",
    "The roof area of the extension hereby permitted shall not be used as a\nbalcony, roof garden or similar amenity area without the grant of further\nspecific permission from the local planning authority.",
    "No window(s)/door(s), other than those shown on the approved\nplans shall be installed in the side elevation(s) of the development hereby\npermitted without the prior permission in writing of the local planning\nauthority. \n\n\n\n\n\n",
    "The\nlandscaping scheme shall be carried out in full accordance with the approved\nLandscaping Plan (Drawing No. 2611/02 Rev A, dated June 2026) within the first\nplanting season following the date of this permission. Any trees, shrubs or\nplants which, within a period of five years from the date of planting, die, are\nremoved, become seriously damaged or diseased, shall be replaced in the next\nplanting season with others of a similar size and species, unless otherwise\nagreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Prior to the first\noccupation of any of the flats hereby approved, the cycle parking facilities\nshown on Drawing No. 2611/02 Rev A (Landscaping Plan, June 2026) shall be\nprovided in full and thereafter retained and kept available for cycle parking\npurposes.",
    "Within three (3)\nmonths of the date of this permission, the boundary treatments comprising\ntimber fencing within the rear gardens and the brick wall along the front\nboundary, as shown on Drawing No. 2611/02 Rev A (Landscaping Plan, June 2026),\nshall be provided in full and thereafter retained and maintained.",
    "The development shall\nbe carried out and retained in accordance with the Fire Safety Strategy\n(Drawing No. 2611/01 Rev A, dated June 2026).",
    "The development hereby\napproved shall be operated and maintained to achieve a maximum water\nconsumption rate of no more than 105 litres per person per day, as set out in\nthe Sustainability Statement (116 Nibthwaite Road, Harrow, dated 7 June 2026),\nand shall be retained as such thereafter.",
    "The\ndevelopment hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the\nfollowing approved plans and documents:  -       Location\nPlan (Drawing L-100 dated August 2023) -       Existing\n(as built) Elevations (Drawing 2412-03 Revision C dated January 2026) -       Existing\n(as built) Floor Plans (Drawing 2210-03 Revision E dated June 2025) -       Landscaping\nPlan (Drawing 2611/02 Revision A dated June 2026) -       Fire\nSafety Strategy (Drawing 2611/01 Revision A dated June 2026) -       Sustainability\nStatement (‘116 Nibthwaite Road, Harrow, H1 1TG, dated 07 June 2026)"
  ],
